; exit 0
; A trait DEFAULT body is checked once per implementing type, over ONE
; AST. This file is the program that proves it, and the subject of
; `scripts/check-fallible-reclaim.sh`'s second half.
;
; `checkImplComplete` synthesizes the default into every impl that
; omits the method without copying the body's nodes, so `ident`'s
; `(match (Some x) ((Some v) v) ((None) x))` is checked twice: once
; with `a` at `String` and once with `a` at `Int`. The binder `v` is
; ONE node, and the two checks disagree about what it holds.
;
; That matters because `stampPatBinderTy` writes the binder's resolved
; type onto that node so codegen can tell a machine scalar - which
; cannot alias the block it was copied out of - from a reference,
; which can (docs/error-model.md ERR-MEM-4). A stamp that took the
; LAST answer would hand `Ident#String#ident` the `Int` written by the
; other impl, and codegen would release the `(Option String)` block
; while `v`, the String inside it, is what the function returns.
;
; SEPARATELY, AND NOT FIXED HERE: the same sharing makes a trait
; default body's SHAPE WORD depend on `impl` declaration order, in the
; compiler as shipped at 0.3.0 and with nothing of ERR-MEM-4's in it.
; Swap the two impls below and `Ident#String#ident` builds its block
; with header `4` - a LEAF, no reference map - and no
; `axiom_retain(%x)`, where this ordering gives header `131076` and the
; retain. One of the two is wrong for `String`; which one, and whether
; any program can observe it, is not established. It is recorded as
; `MM-LIFE-2j` in docs/memory-model.md rather than fixed, because it is
; older than this file and wants its own measurement.
;
; MEASURED 2026-08-25, and this is why the impls are in this order.
; With last-write-wins, `Ident#String#ident` contains
; `call void @axiom_release(i64 %t0)` and with the disagreement
; poisoned it contains none - a one-line IR difference from a one-word
; change in the checker. Swapping the two `impl` declarations moves
; which instantiation gets the wrong answer, and nothing else.
;
; THE PROGRAM ANSWERING CORRECTLY IS NOT THE EVIDENCE, and this file
; says so rather than implying it. It answers correctly under both
; compilers: the released block's field is a String the CALLER still
; holds a share of, so the count reaches 0 in neither. That is luck
; about ownership at the call site, not a property. What this file
; contributes to the corpus is that the shape compiles and runs at all
; - the gate is what reads the IR, because the defect is invisible to
; the program's own output. A fixture asserting only the output would
; be green with the release present, which is the whole reason the
; assertion is not here.
(import IO)

(import Str)

(trait (Ident a) where (
  tag :: (-> a Int)
  ident :: (-> a a) = (lambda (x)
    (match (Some x)
      ((Some v) v)
      ((None) x)))
))

(impl (Ident String) where (
  (tag (lambda (s) (strLen s)))
))

(impl (Ident Int) where (
  (tag (lambda (n) n))
))

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i 200)
        {
          (strLen (ident (strConcat "payload-" (fmtInt i))))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      (println (ident "sentinel"))
      (println (ident 7))
      (println (tag "abc"))
      0
    }
  )
)
